<worksheet >
    <title>EIPO-3 Inner Products</title>
  <introduction>
    <p>To earn an M on this outcome, complete all three problems. 
      Complete part c and one other part to earn a P.</p>
  </introduction>  
   <page>
      <exercise>
        <introduction>
            <p>Let <m>P_2</m> be the vector space of polynomials of degree 2 or less, with the inner product defined by <m>\langle p, q \rangle = \int_{0}^{1} p(x)q(x) \, dx</m>.</p>
        </introduction>
        <task workspace="2in">
            <statement>
                <p>If <m>p(x) = 3x - 1</m> and <m>q(x) = x^2 + 2</m>, calculate the inner product <m>\langle p, q \rangle</m>.</p>
            </statement>
        </task>
        <task workspace="2in">
            <statement>
                <p>Find the norm <m>\|p\|</m> of the polynomial <m>p(x) = 3x - 1</m> using the given inner product.</p>
            </statement>
        </task>
        <task workspace="2in">
            <statement>
                <p>Determine whether the polynomials <m>f(x) = x</m> and <m>g(x) = 3x - 2</m> are orthogonal under this inner product.</p>
            </statement>
        </task>
    </exercise>
  </page>
</worksheet>